What if AI learned physics the way Newton did – by experiencing it? We built Sim2Reason to train LLMs inside virtual worlds governed by real physics laws, with zero human annotation. The result is a 5–10% improvement on the International Physics Olympiad in a zero-shot setting.

@mihirp98: "What if AI learned physics the way Newton did – by experiencing it? We built Sim2Reason: train LLMs inside virtual worlds governed by real physics laws, zero human annotation. Result: +5–10% improvement on International Physics Olympiad, zero-shot."

This is an important achievement, likely the first in a sequence that will lead to fully automating large language model and OMNI training and serving. As someone involved in building multimodal and language models, I believe this will play out in that way.

Remaining challenges include developing environments and applications in critical fields like healthcare, materials science, scientific exploration, and energy harnessing. Solving these could help address issues such as carbon capture and ending hunger.

